{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed","id":906188,"title":"[Whimsy] Soul Claimed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-02T21:22:34-07:00","id":906188,"title":"[Whimsy] Soul Claimed","content":"You know what's interesting? An Idigam with Soul Slave and Forge Claimed. Yes, I <i>know</i> that Soul Slaves aren't Spirits - but let's play pretend for a moment.<br /> <br /> Tear someone's soul out, and make it claim their now Soulless body. You now just gave a random mortal a 15 point Essence Pool, Dread Powers, the ability to Reach, and rapid mutation to look like a mirror of their inner selves. Oh, and they're still Soulless. Because you're either a dick or a magical girl villain.<br /> <hr /><br /> Or Soul Slave and Forge Flesh-Bound Spirit - now that would be <i>interesting</i>. It'd certainly be a lot tougher than the Rank 2 it normally has - it is immune to all wards and protections vs. spirits and ghosts, and it lacks a Ban or Bane...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T07:45:51-07:00","id":906407,"title":"","content":"That is wonderfully diabolical and I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:57:34-07:00","id":906447,"title":"","content":"An Idigam themed around the soul might be an interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:21:27-07:00","id":906465,"title":"","content":"I really like your post, Idigam that use humans to craft horror through the application of existing mechanics is just lovely.<br /> <br /> Question about your signature:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed#post906188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day..</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this meant to be ironic, a use of sarcastic wit, or just something left over from a previous sabbatical from these forums?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:46:18-07:00","id":906484,"title":"","content":"Likely from the previous, though I'd wager I understand them. There are some folks in certain sections of the forums who seem to get off on shitting on people's creativity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:43:04-07:00","id":906877,"title":"","content":"It's left over from a previous sabbatical - I leave it up mostly out of laziness and the recognition that hey, I might leave for good sometime.<br /> <br /> I don't see eye-to-eye with some very prominent posters here - personality conflict, and all that.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> A crossroads devil-style Idigam would be <i>neat</i>.<br /> <br /> I could imagine a Wolf-Blooded pack member that's just so <i>jealous</i> of their Werewolf packmates... but thanks to this deal they were offered, now they can keep up! They're strong and tough enough to be useful on a hunt... and <i>of</i> course their eyes have always been that bright, bright green.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:49:30-07:00","id":906959,"title":"","content":"Boom fomori conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T06:03:47-07:00","id":907074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed#post906188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what's interesting? An Idigam with Soul Slave and Forge Claimed. Yes, I <i>know</i> that Soul Slaves aren't Spirits - but let's play pretend for a moment.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's no need to pretend that forge claimed works with souls, one could just come up with a new power. I remember absolutely nothing saying that those were the only powers idigams can possess, after all.<br /> <br /> You want an idigam that rips the Beast out of vampires to stuff a spirit in them? Go for it.<br /> <br /> You want an idigam whose hobby is stuffing spirits into prometheans to see what happens? Do iiiiiiit. <br /> <br /> You want an idigam that takes souls and spirits and smashes them together to create weird magoth-like things that think like people? All righty then. <br /> <br /> As long as it remotely makes sense considering their specialty is essence, the sky's the limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T18:52:51-07:00","id":907374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed?p=907074#post907074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as it remotely makes sense considering their specialty is essence, the sky's the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally, as Father Moon is there to grab the fuckers if they ever approach it again!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T20:35:15-07:00","id":907412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed?p=907074#post907074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no need to pretend that forge claimed works with souls, one could just come up with a new power. I remember absolutely nothing saying that those were the only powers idigams can possess, after all.<br /> <br /> You want an idigam that rips the Beast out of vampires to stuff a spirit in them? Go for it.<br /> <br /> You want an idigam whose hobby is stuffing spirits into prometheans to see what happens? Do iiiiiiit.<br /> <br /> You want an idigam that takes souls and spirits and smashes them together to create weird magoth-like things that think like people? All righty then.<br /> <br /> As long as it remotely makes sense considering their specialty is essence, the sky's the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to use the pre-existing mechanics. In one of the few times where I <i>don't</i> want to reinvent the wheel.<br /> <br /> (I personally find telling someone whose post count is something like 80% homebrew to make stuff up kinda <i>adorable</i>, but then again, no one reads my stuff, so...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T21:33:23-07:00","id":907441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed#post906188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and rapid mutation to look like a mirror of their inner selves.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would a Storyteller decide what is their &quot;inner selves&quot;? Maybe the Integrity score? The lower, the more warped his features, like a shattered mirror, the higher, the more idealistic, with perfect symmetry and features so &quot;in place&quot; that they look like alien. Virtue and Vice should play a definitive role into this as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed#post906188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it lacks a Ban or Bane...</div> </div> </div> </div>How about creating Bans and Banes based on Virtue and Vice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T04:52:54-07:00","id":907568,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the lower the integrity score, the more obvious the vice becomes, perhaps vice versa with virtue the higher the integrity score? <br /> <br /> As for bans and banes, I'd seriously consider linking them to past integrity breaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:05:58-07:00","id":907861,"title":"","content":"I think you all are over thinking this. How much effort do you usually put into a random npc? I've drifted away from that and it makes it easier to improv.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:16:53-07:00","id":907871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed?p=907861#post907861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you all are over thinking this. How much effort do you usually put into a random npc? I've drifted away from that and it makes it easier to improv.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I wouldn't consider the antagonist of a story a random NPC. Second of all? There's nothing wrong with internal consistency. Third of all, some actors prefer method acting to improv.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T20:25:37-07:00","id":908071,"title":"","content":"1st- a random soul claimed npc ISN'T likely to be the main villain, rather the idigam would be. Second, you can have your consistency, but mulling over full splat sheets for a random that a pc may just as easily decide to eat because 'lawl im monster'. As for 3rd, that's on you, but the story telling rules, as presented for forsaken rely on some level of improv, which is largely refreshing compared to some of the cut and dry storylines people tend to use.<br /> <br /> As an example of over thinking things, the previous posts are &quot;how would we decide what form they'd take? what would it be based on?&quot; Why would you not design the form first, and then form the back story as a second? For inspiration, one could watch season 2 of penny dreadful for dorian grey and how his painting appears. The big thought process should go into the idigam, but with the cannon fodder? work backwards. Even if you don't get that far it's likely the players aren't going to appreciate the amount of effort one put into 'random buy with barbed teeth', and it frees you up to devote more time to world building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 06-05-2016, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:20:44-07:00","id":908102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed?p=908071#post908071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st- a random soul claimed npc ISN'T likely to be the main villain, rather the idigam would be. Second, you can have your consistency, but mulling over full splat sheets for a random that a pc may just as easily decide to eat because 'lawl im monster'. As for 3rd, that's on you, but the story telling rules, as presented for forsaken rely on some level of improv, which is largely refreshing compared to some of the cut and dry storylines people tend to use.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Did I said main villain? No, I said antagonist. Your obnoxious neighbor can be one. The fucker who got irreparably soul-raped could use a bit more of nuance. Finally? If you aren't going to contribute anything to the thread, bow out, please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed?p=908071#post908071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an example of over thinking things, the previous posts are &quot;how would we decide what form they'd take? what would it be based on?&quot; Why would you not design the form first, and then form the back story as a second? For inspiration, one could watch season 2 of penny dreadful for dorian grey and how his painting appears. The big thought process should go into the idigam, but with the cannon fodder? work backwards. Even if you don't get that far it's likely the players aren't going to appreciate the amount of effort one put into 'random buy with barbed teeth', and it frees you up to devote more time to world building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant. We aren't discussing the Idigam here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T19:51:11-07:00","id":908825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/906188-whimsy-soul-claimed?p=907412#post907412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I personally find telling someone whose post count is something like 80% homebrew to make stuff up kinda <i>adorable</i>, but then again, no one reads my stuff, so...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I read your stuff, I've actually saved quite a bit of it and used some of it in games too. For example, I used your genetic vampires merit in a game involving D-Day, WW2, and Natzi vampires-things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}